title: Constitutional Reform
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
view-if: CHP_in_government = 1 and justice_minister_party = "CHP" and constitutional_reform_timer <= 0 and judicial_reform >= 4 and constitutional_reform < 2
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; constitutional_reform_timer = 12
card-image: img/portraits/MuammerAksoy.jpg

= Constitutional Reform

Changes to the rules of parliamentary government need broad support. In this alternate-history scenario, we can seek a two-thirds majority of the 450-seat assembly for an electoral threshold or a constructive vote of no confidence.

- @threshold: Introduce a 5% national electoral threshold.
- @confidence: Require a proposed replacement government for a vote of no confidence.
- @root: Leave the rules unchanged.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@threshold
view-if: electoral_threshold = 0
choose-if: progressive_coalition >= 300
unavailable-subtitle: We need 300 supporting seats in the assembly.
on-arrival: electoral_threshold = 5; constitutional_reform += 1; kemalist_marxists_dissent += 10; TIP_relation -= 5
achievement: constitutional_reform

The assembly passes the electoral threshold. Smaller parties oppose the change; future elections will apply the new rule.

@confidence
view-if: constructive_vonc = 0
choose-if: progressive_coalition >= 300
unavailable-subtitle: We need 300 supporting seats in the assembly.
on-arrival: constructive_vonc = 1; constitutional_reform += 1
achievement: constitutional_reform

The assembly requires confidence votes to identify a replacement government, reducing the risk of a parliamentary deadlock.
